  "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements disabled-by-default missed-callback recovery for known PlaceToPay sessions and PayPhone sales. This is a dependent payment-core increment, not provider qualification or completion of the whole payments platform.\n\n- Add durable per-operation query jobs, bounded attempts/backoff, two-minute leases and terminal-history guards.\n- Share a PostgreSQL query-reservation budget between callbacks and scheduled queries, across replicas.\n- Query the original immutable resource only; never create/capture/refund/void/payout or switch providers from this worker.\n- Recheck the live lease and account/flag authority before atomically committing the job outcome with payment, intent, ledger, receipt and audit changes.\n- Dead-letter exhausted/mismatched/conflicting evidence for review without inferring no charge or fabricating inbox evidence.\n- Add 35 database cases, migration rollback checks, ADR 0120 and detailed operator/test evidence.\n\n## Dependencies / review order\n\nBase: #358 (`a5ba14f0be4e4f6da1df666b31dd6ae343afedab`).\n\nReview after #331 \u2192 #332 \u2192 #334 \u2192 #340 \u2192 #343 \u2192 #347 \u2192 #350 \u2192 #353 \u2192 #358. Staging #344 is a separate sibling after #343. Do not merge this PR ahead of its dependencies. No merge, production deployment or live transaction is authorized.\n\n## Verified local tests\n\nSource: runtime/test commit `ddfc19eb9247bf539a676755986cb5e5369d8f3b`, catalog-only follow-up `7f8633050a5123559823ccdcd6fc6c1923a7d22a`. Subsequent changes are documentation only. Local macOS, Stack lts-24.42/GHC 9.10.3 and disposable PostgreSQL 16; synthetic provider transport only.\n\n- `stack test --fast --rerun-tests`: **2,589 examples, zero failures**, 44.6360 seconds.\n- `sh scripts/test-provider-retry-runtime.sh`: **107 examples, zero failures**, 52.0003 seconds; includes 35 new worker cases and 72 inherited regressions.\n- Harness repeat-apply, empty rollback/reapply, operator-edited flag preservation and used-history rollback refusal/read-back: passed. Owned disposable containers removed and absence verified.\n- Production release/entrypoint Node tests: **60 passed**.\n- Catalog scanner regression: **one passed**. Final catalog gate: **1,416 files / 1,125 candidates / zero unreviewed or stale decisions**. Gate/scanner unchanged; three fixed protocol reviews plus migration-manifest fingerprint refreshed.\n- Manifest introducer ancestry/SQL identity, migration-batch rendering, shell syntax, relative doc links and whitespace checks passed.\n\nAn earlier DB run had two fixture-query ambiguity failures; both were fixed before the final run. An initial catalog review marker error was corrected without relaxing the gate. Exact commands, timestamps, intermediate failures and scope are recorded in [verification/runbook](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/139a45102c4b715cc8762b5653d0a2db061b167c/docs/payments/query-recovery-2026-09-15.md).\n\nNo real provider sandbox, staging payment, browser/device E2E or complete production-schema rehearsal was run for this increment. Parent CI passed its active gates; new PR CI is not inferred from that result.\n\n## Migration / rollout / rollback\n\nAdditive migration `2026-09-15_provider_query_recovery.sql`, introduced by `b9875ff176c35f446c64d53dccadfd15b839cda4`, is appended to the reviewed migration manifest. No historical payment/provider reference backfill or rewrite.\n\n**Apply schema before updated callback binaries:** callbacks now require the shared budget table even when scheduled recovery is disabled. Drain old callback consumers before worker activation; they do not reserve this budget.\n\nBoth exact `checkout.provider_query_recovery` environment flags default false. `COMMERCE_PROVIDER_QUERY_RECOVERY_ENABLED` must be exactly `true`, the checkout environment explicit, the original merchant account qualified and the runtime adapter configured. None was activated here.\n\nDisable worker gates before rollback. Retain used schema/history; the rollback refuses if either new table contains rows and deletes only untouched false flag seeds on an unused installation. Never clear rows to force rollback. Reverting callback code removes the shared-budget guarantee.\n\n## Risks / remaining blockers\n\n- Staging health is reachable, but all six hosting inspections report authentication unavailable; deployed SHA/provider qualification are unknown. Approved app-scoped hosting access and genuine sandbox accounts/contracts/method mappings/webhook registration are still required.\n- Quota coordination covers this database only. Confirm PayPhone's documented quota scope and coordinate external integrations sharing credentials before activation.\n- Unknown-resource ambiguous creates, late-paid/expired fulfillment, safe dead-letter reprocessing/admin controls and PayPhone's inherited canceled-as-declined compatibility fix remain follow-up work.\n- Broader recurring/mandate, refund/void, settlement/dispute, tax/SRI and compliant connected-seller payout work remains. No legal/accounting/PCI certification is claimed.\n\nNo API/generated-client/web/mobile/admin source changes or screenshots in this increment. [ADR 0120](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/139a45102c4b715cc8762b5653d0a2db061b167c/docs/adr/0120-durable-provider-query-recovery.md) contains the state flow, threat controls and transaction/activation boundaries.\n",
